# The KF5 runner talks to the old fixed socket path and silently spawns a second
# GUI against 0.9.11 -- force it out; the KF6 runner depends on >= 0.9.11 anyway.
Breaks: openfortigui-runner (<< 0.9.11)
Description: Qt GUI for openfortivpn, a Fortinet SSL-VPN client
 openfortiGUI manages several Fortinet SSL-VPN connections and groups of
 connections. openfortivpn is built in, so no separate client is needed: the
 privileged part of a connection is started through sudo while the interface
 keeps running as the ordinary user.
 .
 A tray icon shows the state of every connection. Prompts for one-time passwords
 and for the passphrase of an encrypted client certificate are answered in a
 dialog, gateway certificates can be pinned, and credentials can be kept in the
 system keyring instead of the configuration file. A KRunner plugin is packaged
 separately.
